   <section xml:id=3D"section-scalar-negation">
     <title>Scalar Negation</title>
     <para>Let us now consider some other types of negation. For example, w=
hen we say:</para>
     <example xml:id=3D"example-random-id-GJga">
       <title>
         <anchor xml:id=3D"c15e3d1"/>
       </title>
-        <para>The chair is not brown.</para>
+      <para>The chair is not brown.</para>
     </example>
     <para>we make a positive inference - that the chair is some other colo=
r. Thus, it is legitimate to respond:</para>
     <example xml:id=3D"example-random-id-DDN8">
       <title>
         <anchor xml:id=3D"c15e3d2"/>
