     </example>
     <para>although these would clarify the vague negation. Another circuml=
ocution for English scalar negation is=20
     <quote>other than</quote>, which works where=20
     <quote>non-</quote> does not, but is wordier.</para>
     <para>Finally, we have natural language negations that are called pola=
r negations, or opposites:</para>
     <example xml:id=3D"example-random-id-qh2s">
